<%- else -%>
<%- if @method.constructor? -%>
*(Ruby's default constructor; documents `#initialize`.)*

<%- end -%>
<%- overloads = @method.tags(:overload) -%>
<%-
  # +primary+ is @method's sole @overload tag when there are 0 or 1 (nil for
  # 0, meaning "no overload tag at all — fall back to @method's own real
  # params/return"); nil when there are 2+, since each overload then
  # documents its own params/return inline instead of collapsing to one
  # shared signature. Shared by both branches below and, further down, by
  # the Returns section in the tail, which re-tests +overloads.size < 2+ to
  # know whether +primary+ (as opposed to per-overload Returns already
  # rendered above) applies.
-%>
<%- primary = overloads.size < 2 ? overloads.first : nil -%>
<%- if overloads.size >= 2 -%>
```ruby
<%- overloads.each do |ov| -%>
<%= signature_text(@method, overload: ov) %>
<%- end -%>
```
<%- prose = erb(:method_prose).strip -%>
<%- unless prose.empty? -%>

<%= prose %>
<%- end -%>
<%- overloads.each do |ov| -%>

**`<%= signature_text(@method, overload: ov) %>`**
<%- ov_param_tags = ordered_param_tags(@method, ov.tags(:param), overload: ov) -%>
<%- unless ov_param_tags.empty? -%>

**Params:**

<%- ov_param_tags.each do |p| -%>
- `<%= p.name %>` (<%= type_ref_first(p) %>)<%= summary_suffix(p.text) %>
<%- end -%>
<%- end -%>
<%- ov_return = ov.tag(:return) -%>
<%- if ov_return -%>

**Returns:**

- <%= dash_join(type_ref_first(ov_return), ov_return.text) %>
<%- end -%>
<%- end -%>
<%- else -%>
```ruby
<%= signature_text(@method, overload: primary) %>
```
<%- prose = erb(:method_prose).strip -%>
<%- unless prose.empty? -%>

<%= prose %>
<%- end -%>
<%- param_tags = ordered_param_tags(@method, primary ? primary.tags(:param) : @method.tags(:param), overload: primary) -%>
<%- unless param_tags.empty? -%>

**Params:**

<%- param_tags.each do |p| -%>
- `<%= p.name %>` (<%= type_ref_first(p) %>)<%= summary_suffix(p.text) %>
<%- end -%>
<%- option_tags = @method.tags(:option) -%>
<%- param_tags.each do |p| -%>
<%- opts = option_tags.select { |o| o.name == p.name } -%>
<%- next if opts.empty? -%>

**Options (`<%= p.name %>`):**

<%- opts.each do |o| -%>
<%= option_line(o) %>
<%- end -%>
<%- end -%>
<%- end -%>
<%- end -%>
<%- yt = yield_tag(@method) -%>
<%- if yt -%>
<%- yt_names = yt.types || [] -%>

**Yields:**

- <%= dash_join(yt_names.empty? ? "" : yt_names.map { |n| "`#{n}`" }.join(', '), yt.text) %>
<%- end -%>
<%- unless @method.tags(:yieldparam).empty? -%>

**Yield Params:**

<%- @method.tags(:yieldparam).each do |p| -%>
- `<%= p.name %>` (<%= type_ref_first(p) %>)<%= summary_suffix(p.text) %>
<%- end -%>
<%- end -%>
<%- yieldreturn_tags = @method.tags(:yieldreturn) -%>
<%- unless yieldreturn_tags.empty? -%>

**Yield Returns:**

<%- yieldreturn_tags.each do |yrt| -%>
- <%= dash_join(type_ref(yrt.types && yrt.types.join(", ")), yrt.text) %>
<%- end -%>
<%- end -%>
<%-
  # No top-level Returns section when overloads.size >= 2 (+primary+ is nil
  # then): each overload already rendered its own Returns above, so there's
  # nothing left for @method's own tags to contribute here.
-%>
<%- return_tags = overloads.size < 2 ? (primary ? primary.tags(:return) : method_return_tags(@method)) : [] -%>
<%- unless return_tags.empty? -%>

**Returns:**

<%- return_tags.each do |rt| -%>
- <%= dash_join(type_ref(rt.types && rt.types.join(", ")), rt.text) %>
<%- end -%>
<%- end -%>
<%- unless @method.tags(:raise).empty? -%>

**Raises:**

<%- @method.tags(:raise).each do |r| -%>
- <%= dash_join(type_ref_first(r), r.text) %>
<%- end -%>
<%- end -%>
<%- unless @method.tags(:see).empty? -%>

**See also:**

<%- @method.tags(:see).each do |t| -%>
- <%= dash_join(see_ref(t), t.text) %>
<%- end -%>
<%- end -%>
